WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.220
In this lesson, you will learn to use operator blocks (+ − × ÷ and join) to calculate, and check a typed answer against the right result.

2
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.030
Green operator blocks do maths: + − × ÷.

3
00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:18.140
They go inside other blocks, like a calculator inside your code.

4
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:22.690
In Scratch, × is written *.

5
00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:26.010
Compare what the player typed with the right answer using =.

6
00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:31.040
If they match, the answer is correct.

7
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:39.470
“join” glues words and numbers together so a sprite can say a whole sentence, like “Total: 7”.

8
00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:41.590
Store a number in a variable, then do maths with it later.

9
00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:50.250
That is how calculators and games keep track of things.

10
00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.200
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

11
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:58.330
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
